+## Troubleshooting
+
+### MCP Timeout Issues
+
+If agents timeout during MCP calls, increase timeout in agent configuration:
+
+File: `agents/*/agent.py:69`
+```python
+timeout_seconds=30,  # Increase if needed
+```
+
+### API Quota Exhaustion (429 Errors)
+
+The system automatically retries with exponential backoff. If errors persist:
+- Check GOOGLE_API_KEY is valid
+- Wait for quota reset
+- Consider using Vertex AI instead
+
+### Agent Not Loading
+
+1. Check agent is running: `lsof -i :10101`
+2. Verify agent card: `curl http://localhost:10101/.well-known/agent-card.json`
+3. Check logs: `tail -f /tmp/technical_analyst.log`
+
+### Infinite Loading in UI
+
+This usually indicates:
+- Agent crashed or timed out
+- MCP server not accessible
+- API quota exceeded
+
+Check agent logs for error details.
+
+## Important Patterns
+
+### Adding a New Specialized Agent
+
+1. Create new directory: `agents/new_specialist/`
+2. Copy structure from existing agent
+3. Update `agent.py` with specialist prompt
+4. Add to workspace: `pyproject.toml`
+5. Update `run_all.sh` to start new agent
+6. Update Host Agent instruction to include new specialist
+
+### Modifying Analysis Output
+
+To change report format:
+1. Update agent instructions: `agents/*/agent.py`
+2. Update synthesis template: `hosts/multiagent/host_agent.py:179-235`
+3. Ensure JSON extraction still works: `hosts/multiagent/host_agent.py:518-530`
+
+### Changing LLM Model
+
+Update model in agent configurations:
+```python
+# Current: gemini-2.0-flash-001
+model=Gemini(model='gemini-2.0-flash-001', api_key=os.getenv('GOOGLE_API_KEY'))
+```
+
+Or use LiteLLM for other providers:
+```python
+from google.adk.models.lite_llm import LiteLlm
+model=LiteLlm(model='gemini/gemini-2.0-flash-001')
+```
+
+## Documentation References
+
+- **Business Logic**: `docs/AGENT_ARCHITECTURE.md`
+- **Technical Design**: `docs/SYSTEM_DESIGN.md`
+- **Verification Guide**: `docs/VERIFICATION_GUIDE.md`
+- **Google A2A Protocol**: https://google.github.io/A2A/
+- **Google ADK**: https://google.github.io/adk-docs/
+
+## Development Philosophy
+
+This codebase follows a **minimal modification** strategy:
+- Use existing open-source MCP servers (don't reinvent the wheel)
+- Keep demo UI unchanged from upstream
+- Minimal Host Agent changes (~100 lines for multi-agent coordination)
+- Configuration over code (use .env for all settings)
+- Clear separation: MCP (data) vs A2A (intelligence) vs Host (orchestration)
